    "result_text": "The full suite is green \u2014 `AcceptanceTest` is the only test class in the project, and `BUILD SUCCESS` confirms compilation (including the generated OpenAPI interface) and the test pass.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented idempotent owner creation in `OwnerRestControllerV1` (`src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java`), the controller behind `POST /api/owners`.\n\n**Behavior:** When a create request carries an `Idempotency-Key` header whose key has already produced an owner, the endpoint returns that original owner with **200 OK** instead of running the creation path again (which would otherwise 409 on the duplicate-identity check). A first/unseen key creates normally and still returns **201 Created**.\n\n**Changes:**\n- Added an in-memory `ConcurrentHashMap<String, Integer> ownersByIdempotencyKey` mapping each seen key to the id of the owner it created.\n- At the top of `addOwner`, look up the current request's `Idempotency-Key`; on a hit, fetch that owner and return it with 200.\n- After a successful `saveOwner`, record `key \u2192 owner.getId()`.\n- Added `currentIdempotencyKey()`, which reads the header via `RequestContextHolder`/`ServletRequestAttributes`. I used this rather than adding a `@RequestHeader` parameter because `addOwner` overrides the OpenAPI-generated `OwnersApi` interface, whose signature has no header parameter \u2014 this keeps the generated contract untouched. The helper returns `null` when the header is absent/blank, so existing keyless creates are unaffected.\n\nA note on scope: the store is a per-instance in-memory map, which satisfies the spec and test within a single application instance but does not survive restarts or coordinate across multiple instances. If you need durable/cluster-wide idempotency, that would call for persisting the key (e.g. a table or shared cache) \u2014 happy to extend it if that's in scope.",
