    "probe_text": "`POST /api/owners` is handled by `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner(OwnerFieldsDto)` (`src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java:148-214`). Here is everything it applies, in execution order. I've tagged each step as **[V]** validation (can reject the request) or **[S]** side-effect (mutation / persistence / derived state).\n\n### Authorization\n1. **[V]** `@PreAuthorize(\"hasRole(@roles.OWNER_ADMIN)\")` \u2014 caller must hold the `OWNER_ADMIN` role, else the request is rejected before the method body runs (line 148).\n\n### Idempotency short-circuit (before any validation)\n2. **[S/V]** Reads the `Idempotency-Key` request header (`currentIdempotencyKey`, line 151). If it's present, was seen before, and the owner it produced still exists, the method **returns that existing owner with `200 OK` and creates nothing** (lines 152-160). Otherwise it proceeds.\n\n### Required-field validation (accumulated, reported together)\n3. **[V]** `firstName` must be non-blank (line 162).\n4. **[V]** `lastName` must be non-blank (line 163).\n5. **[S]** Normalizes `addressLine1`, `addressLine2`, and the flat `address` (trim, collapse whitespace, upper-case, expand `ST/RD/AVE`); composes a single `normalizedAddress` \u2014 preferring the structured lines when `addressLine1` is present, else the flat address (lines 164-171).\n6. **[V]** The composed `address` must be non-blank (line 171).\n7. **[V]** `city` must be non-blank (line 172).\n8. **[V]** `telephone` must be non-blank (line 173).\n9. **[V]** If any of the above are missing \u2192 throw `MissingRequiredFieldsException` listing all offending fields (lines 174-176).\n\n### Field-value validation\n10. **[V]** `validatePostcode` (line 177): if a postcode is supplied it must be exactly 4 digits, and for a city with a known region (NSW/VIC/QLD) it must fall in that region's range (2000-2099 / 3000-3099 / 4000-4099). Absent postcode is allowed.\n11. **[V]** `validateRegistrationDate` (line 178): if a registration date is supplied it must not be later than today.\n\n### Registration-date derivation + rate/capacity limits\n12. **[S]** Effective date = supplied date, else `LocalDate.now()` (lines 179-180).\n13. **[S]** `toBusinessDay` rolls that date forward past Saturdays, Sundays, and listed public holidays to the next business day (line 181).\n14. **[V]** `requireDailyLimitNotReached` (line 182): if \u2265100 owners already carry that business-day registration date \u2192 `DailyOwnerLimitException`.\n15. **[V]** `requireCityBelowCapacity` (line 183): if the city already has \u226550 owners (case-insensitive) \u2192 `CityAtCapacityException`.\n\n### Telephone / email normalization\n16. **[V/S]** `normalizeTelephone` converts telephone to E.164 (strips spaces/dashes/brackets, assumes `+61` when no `+`, enforces 8-15 digits plus AU=9 / NANP=10 national-length rules); invalid \u2192 `InvalidFieldValueException`. The normalized value is written back onto the DTO (lines 184-185).\n17. **[V/S]** If `email` is present, `normalizeEmail` validates it against the email pattern (invalid \u2192 `InvalidFieldValueException`), lower-cases it, and rejects disposable domains (`mailinator.com`, `tempmail.com`, `guerrillamail.com` \u2192 `InvalidFieldValueException`). Canonical value written back onto the DTO (lines 186-188).\n\n### Map to entity + derive stored fields\n18. **[S]** Reads `sharesHousehold` flag (line 189).\n19. **[S]** Maps DTO \u2192 `Owner` via `ownerMapper.toOwner` (line 191).\n20. **[S]** Sets `address` = normalized address; sets `addressLine1`/`addressLine2` (null when unstructured or line2 empty) (lines 192-195).\n21. **[S]** Sets `registrationDate` = the business-day-adjusted date (line 196).\n22. **[S]** Sets `customerCode` via `buildCustomerCode`: `<REGION>-<8-hex SHA-256 of telephone+lastName>`, de-duplicated with a `-2`, `-3`\u2026 suffix against all existing owners' codes (line 197).\n23. **[S]** Sets `namesakeCount` = count of existing owners matching first+last name case-insensitively (line 198).\n24. **[S]** Sets `householdId` = 12-hex SHA-256 of normalized `lastName + \"|\" + postcode`, or `null` when there's no postcode (line 199).\n\n### Duplicate checks\n25. **[V]** `requireUniqueIdentity` (line 200): if the owner's `identityKey` (`telephone|email|householdId`) exactly matches any **non-deleted** existing owner \u2192 `DuplicateIdentityException`.\n26. **[V]** `requireNoHouseholdDuplicate` (line 201): unless `sharesHousehold` is true, if any non-deleted owner already has the same `householdId` \u2192 `DuplicateIdentityException` (owners with no `householdId` are exempt).\n27. **[S]** `markPossibleDuplicate` (line 202): clears the flags, then (unless `sharesHousehold`, and only when a `householdId` exists) if another owner shares the household but has a different telephone, sets `possibleDuplicate = true` and `possibleDuplicateOf` = the earliest such owner's id.\n\n### Persistence + post-save side-effects\n28. **[S]** `clinicService.saveOwner(owner)` \u2014 persists the owner (line 203).\n29. **[S]** If an idempotency key was supplied, records `key \u2192 owner.id` in the in-memory map for future replays (lines 204-206).\n30. **[S]** Builds the response `OwnerDto` (`toOwnerDtoWithBulkWarning`), which additionally computes the `bulkSignupWarning` flag (>80 owners on the registration date) and recomputes `membershipPoints`/`membershipLevel` using the real household size (line 207). Mapping also derives many read-only fields (display name, salutation, telephone display, initials, `membershipNumber`, `fiscalYear`, `checkDigit`, locality, timezone, contact preference, identity key, age band, self link).\n31. **[S]** Writes an `AUDIT` log line recording id, customer code, registration date, membership level and number (lines 208-210).\n32. **[S]** Sets the `Location` response header to `/api/owners/{id}` and returns `201 CREATED` (lines 211-213).\n\nA few things worth flagging about the ordering:\n- The **idempotency replay (step 2) happens before all validation**, so a replayed key returns the cached owner even if the (ignored) body would now be invalid.\n- **Duplicate/identity checks (25-26) ignore soft-deleted owners** (`isDeleted`), so a duplicate is allowed if the only match was soft-deleted.\n- Several checks are **read-modify-write against `findAllOwners()` without locking** (daily limit, city capacity, customer-code dedup, identity/household uniqueness), so they are point-in-time and race-prone under concurrent creates."
